# AI-agent development-template scaffolding (Claude Code / VS Code Copilot).
# This is local workflow tooling for building markharness, not part of the
# released product or something an external contributor needs to read; the
# substantive rules it carries (build/test commands, license/versioning
# policy, docs layout) are published instead in README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md,
# SECURITY.md, and docs/. Keep this block minimal: only ignore whole
# directories/files that are purely template/agent plumbing, never `docs/`,
# `.github/workflows/`, `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/`, or `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`,
# which are real project infrastructure.
